<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wesel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wesel is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, where the Lippe joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. A Hanseatic town in the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a>, it became a refuge for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Calvinists in the 16th century and later a major Prussian fortress. It was almost totally destroyed in 1945 during the Allied crossing of the Rhine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wesel.jpg" alt="Wesel" width="320" height="491" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Peter Schaefer (http://www.reserv-a-rt.de) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wesel_willibrordi_dom_chor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
